  "title": "SIKH EMPIRE: AR gobindshahi rupee (6.17g), Anandgarh, VS1844. VF-EF",
  "description": "SIKH EMPIRE: AR gobindshahi rupee (6.17g), Anandgarh, VS1844, KM-30, Herrli-02.02.04, contemporary imitation, extremely light, whereas a normal gobindshahi rupee of Anandgarh should weigh about 11.10g, 3 testmarks, appears to have been struck from worn official dies, VF to EF, ex Jess A. Yockers Collection.    Actual Anandgarh rupees, struck VS1841-1849, vary considerably in weight, with high grade examples varying from about 10.6g to 11.4g. Contemporary high grade rupees of Amritsar dated in the VS1840s follow a narrow range of about 11.12g to 11.27g.",
